C - Exchange Axiom

Exchange is the shifting of perspective. The Exchange / Permutation Axiom swaps the order of two arguments for a function.
C f x y = f y x.

🌊

@[ts]

// 🔗 Implicit Gravity: No imports required. Dependencies are in the DNA.
export const C = <A, B, C>(f: (x: A) => (y: B) => C) => (y: B) => (x: A): C => f(x)(y);


@[rs]

// 🔗 Native implementation
pub fn C<A, B, C, F>(f: F, y: B, x: A) -> C
where
    F: Fn(A) -> Box<dyn Fn(B) -> C>,
{
    f(x)(y)
}


